    "post_provisioning_notes": {
      "value": "Terraform apply completion means OCI instances, VNICs, and IPs were created; Windows first-boot automation continues afterward. Wait at least 10-15 minutes before testing, and on a fresh deployment allow the DC promotion cycle to finish first (often 20-25 minutes). Verify DOMAIN_READY.txt on DC-VM, WINDOWS_BOOTSTRAP_READY.txt on both SQL nodes, WSFC_READY.txt on SQL1, and TASK_5_5_LISTENER_READY.txt on both SQL nodes before using the RDP IPs or testing AOAG. DC-VM first-boot user_data configures mssqlaoag.demo, creates domainadmin, creates sqlsa, and creates \\\\DC-VM.mssqlaoag.demo\\ClusterWitness. SQL1/SQL2 first-boot user_data joins the domain, installs SQL Server/SSMS when enabled, prepares WSFC/Always On, creates the file-share witness, restores AdventureWorks2025 with NORECOVERY on SQL2, creates TestAOAG, waits for synchronization, and configures the native AOAG-LSN listener on port 1433 with 10.0.20.30 and 10.0.30.30 when auto_configure_wsfc is true. The next manual step is listener connectivity and failover validation.",
      "type": "string"
    },
